s7-2-p4 : Block
s7-2-p4 = prose (cons "A memory model is a predicate \(\mathsf{Allowed}(X)\) selecting permitted executions. A data race, a happens-before relation, or an atomic ordering constraint is a property of these relations. A compiler correctness theorem for concurrent programs must relate the admitted target executions to the admitted source executions. Matching the behavior of each isolated instruction is insufficient when reordering and weak memory are observable." nil)
